This directory contains various "canned" versions of h/ansi/float.h.  The
comment at the top of each file notes which floating-point hardware the file
has been tested on.

If one of these is directly usable in your environment, then copy or link it
to h/ansi/float.h.

Otherwise, copy the one that most closely approximates your configuration into
h/ansi/float.h and edit it appropriately.  If your distribution of IPW
includes the program "machine" (see src/etc/machine), then you may be able to
use it to generate a float.h automatically.

Once your new float.h works, please mail a copy of it to "ipw@crseo.ucsb.edu"
so we can incorporate it into the standard distribution.  Be sure that the
comment at the top of the file adequately describes your particular operating
system and hardware.

macros:

FLT_RADIX	("b") radix of exponent representation

FLT_ROUNDS	addition rounds (> 0, implementation-dependent), chops (0), or
			indeterminable (-1)

FLT_MANT_DIG	("p") number of base-b digits in the floating-point mantissa
DBL_MANT_DIG
LDBL_MANT_DIG

FLT_EPSILON	minimum positive floating-point number x such that
DBL_EPSILON		1.0 + x != 1.0
LDBL_EPSILON

FLT_DIG		number of decimal digits of precision:
DBL_DIG			if b == 10 then	p
LDBL_DIG		else (p - 1) * log10(b)

FLT_MIN_EXP	("emin") minimum negative integer such that b**(emin - 1) is a
DBL_MIN_EXP		normalized floating-point number
LDBL_MIN_EXP

FLT_MIN		minimum normalized positive floating-point number:
DBL_MIN			b**(emin - 1)
LDBL_MIN

FLT_MIN_10_EXP	minimum negative integer such that 10 raised to that power is
DBL_MIN_10_EXP		in the range of normalized floating-point numbers
LDBL_MIN_10_EXP

FLT_MAX_EXP	("emax") maximum integer such that b**(emax - 1) is a
DBL_MAX_EXP		representable finite floating-point number
LDBL_MAX_EXP

FLT_MAX		maximum representable finite floating-point number:
DBL_MAX			(1 - b**-p) * b**emax
LDBL_MAX

FLT_MAX_10_EXP	maximum integer such that 10 raised to that power is in the
DBL_MAX_10_EXP		range of representable finite floating-point numbers
LDBL_MAX_10_EXP

